## Summary of D&D 5e Character Sheet Systems

Based on my thorough exploration of `/Users/alexhedtke/Documents/dnd-character-sheet/Character Sheet.html`, here is the precise mapping of the relevant systems for your multiclass wizard rework:

---

### 1. ASI "Owed/Overdue" Alert System

**Data Structures** (lines 1281–1282):
```javascript
let asiChoices = [];                         // {type:"asi"|"feat"|"", ab1, ab2, feat, source:"class"|"race", featAbil}
let asiFeatsAdded = {};                      // feat names already written to Features (avoid dupes)
```
`asiChoices` is indexed 0..n, each slot tracks: type (empty/"asi"/"feat"), ability picks (ab1/ab2), selected feat, feat ability (for half-feats), and source ("class" or "race").

**ASI Computation** (lines 1359–1373):
- `classAsiLevels(cls)` — returns array of levels at which the class grants ASI (line 1359). Fighter gets `[4,6,8,12,14,16,19]`, Rogue gets `[4,8,10,12,16,19]`, others get `[4,8,12,16,19]`.
- `asiCount()` (line 1366) — parses `$("classlevel").value` with regex `/([A-Za-z''][A-Za-z''\- ]*?)\s+(\d+)/g` to extract class-level pairs (handles multiclass!), sums ASI slots owed. Falls back to single-class interpretation if no regex match.

**ASI Slot Sync** (lines 1393–1401):
```javascript
function syncAsiSlots(){
  const nClass = asiCount(), nRace = raceFeatGrants();
  const classSlots = asiChoices.filter(s => s.source !== "race");
  const raceSlots  = asiChoices.filter(s => s.source === "race");
  while(classSlots.length < nClass) classSlots.push({type:"", ab1:"", ab2:"", feat:"", source:"class"});
  if(classSlots.length > nClass) classSlots.length = nClass;
  while(raceSlots.length < nRace) raceSlots.push({type:"feat", ab1:"", ab2:"", feat:"", source:"race"});
  if(raceSlots.length > nRace) raceSlots.length = nRace;
  asiChoices = classSlots.concat(raceSlots);
}
```
Keeps existing choices when resizing.

**Bonus Application** (lines 1404–1438):
- `applyAsiBonuses()` — iterates `asiChoices`, applying ability increases to `bonusVals.asi` (per slot type), and one-time feat additions (Features text, saves proficiencies, senses). See lines 1407–1438.

**Alert/Flag Rendering** (lines 1453–1467):
```javascript
function updateAsiFlag(){
  syncAsiSlots();
  const flag = $("asi-flag"); if(!flag) return;
  const pendingClass = asiChoices.filter(s => s.source !== "race" && !asiSlotComplete(s)).length;
  const pendingRace  = asiChoices.filter(s => s.source === "race" && !asiSlotComplete(s)).length;
  const pending = pendingClass + pendingRace;
  if(pending > 0){
    const parts = [];
    if(pendingClass) parts.push(pendingClass + " Ability Score Improvement" + (pendingClass>1?"s":""));
    if(pendingRace)  parts.push(pendingRace + " racial feat" + (pendingRace>1?"s":""));
    flag.style.display = "";
    flag.innerHTML = "⚠ " + parts.join(" + ") + " to assign"+
      "<span class=\"sub\">Click to choose an ASI (+2/+1+1) or a Feat for each.</span>";
  } else flag.style.display = "none";
}
```
Flag HTML element: `id="asi-flag"` (line 664, styled line 174–181). Rendered on main sheet when `pending > 0`. Clears when all slots are filled (`asiSlotComplete()` checks type is set + ability/feat picks complete).

**Completion Check** (lines 1374–1384):
```javascript
function asiSlotComplete(s){
  if(!s || !s.type) return false;
  if(s.type === "asi")  return !!(s.ab1 || s.ab2);
  if(s.type === "feat"){
    if(!s.feat) return false;
    const f = DATA && DATA.feats && DATA.feats.find(x => x.name === s.feat);
    if(f && f.ability && f.ability.choose && !s.featAbil) return false;   // half-feat: must pick which ability
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

