blocks.text:
**The bug:** The wizard's starting-equipment step expands weapon-category options ("any martial weapon") via `weaponsFor()`, which filtered only by category and melee/ranged. It never applied the futuristic filter, so laser/antimatter weapons leaked into those dropdowns even with the Settings toggle off. The main inventory autocomplete (`availableItemNames()`) already filtered them, but this code path didn't.

**The fix** (`Character Sheet.html`, `weaponsFor`): exclude any weapon whose name is in `DATA.futuristic` unless `showFuturistic` is on — same name-set the inventory autocomplete uses:

```js
function weaponsFor(slot){
  const fut = showFuturistic ? null : new Set((DATA && DATA.futuristic) || []);
  return ((DATA && DATA.weapons) || []).filter(w => w.cat === slot.cat && (!slot.melee || (slot.melee === "melee" ? w.melee : !w.melee)) && (!fut || !fut.has(w.name)));
}
```

No `build-data.py` change needed — `weaponsFor` is UI-only, and the `futuristic` extraction (`build_futuristic`) already exists. The only tracked change is the two-line edit to `Character Sheet.html`.

Want me to commit and push this?

